Debugging a movement feel problem, you add one field to the replicated set so you can see it on the client:

    [GhostField(Quantization = 1000)] public float3 Velocity;

It ships, because it was useful and nobody remembered to take it out. Two hundred ghosts of this type. No error, no warning, no measurable client CPU change, and the ghost still replicates correctly.
